==Ranks==
The ordinary Qymish nobility is divided into six ranks. From highest to lowest, these are: [[wikipedia:duke|duke]], [[wikipedia:marquess|marquess]], [[wikipedia:count|count]], [[wikipedia:viscount|viscount]], [[wikipedia:baron|baron]], and [[wikipedia:lord|lord]], as well as the feminine forms of these titles. 

===Prince/Princess===
{{See|List of current Qymish princes and princesses}}

Princes and princesses are direct members of the royal family's male lines, or acquire the title through marriage. It is to be noted that only women, in other words wives of princes, can be granted the title of princess through marriage, and they can only use that title if they take their husband's full name. 

