Lords and ladies are the consolidated title for all hereditary nobility in Qym besides princes and princesses, as established by the [[Fundamental Law of Qym]]. U/C 

===Sir/Dame===
{{Main|List of knights in Qymish nobility}}

People who received a knighthood are referred to as sir or dame. U/C

==Succession==
Succession to Qymish noble titles is hereditary for princes and lords, but not automatic. Other titles are not hereditary, including dukes, marquess, counts, viscounts, and barons, which are all nobility titles granted by the [[King of Qym]] to the lords or ladies who are appointed to be the executive of various administrative divisions, as established by the [[Fundamental Law of Qym]]. Knighthoods are also not hereditary, as they are based upon the merit of an individual's life achievements, and not their descendants.

